<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Cybersecurity Master Knowledge Base</title><style>
body{font-family:system-ui;background:#0d1117;color:#e6edf3;margin:0;padding:24px}
h1{color:#58a6ff} h2{color:#79c0ff;border-bottom:1px solid #30363d;padding-top:28px;margin-top:36px}
h3{color:#c9d1d9;margin:20px 0 10px}
.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(340px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-bottom:16px}
.card{background:#161b22;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:8px;padding:12px}
.nm{font-weight:700;color:#f0f6fc;font-size:14px}
.lv{display:inline-block;font-size:10px;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:10px;color:#0d1117;font-weight:700;margin-left:6px}
.mt{font-size:12px;color:#8b949e;margin-top:4px}
.kc{font-size:11px;color:#58a6ff;margin-top:4px}
.df{font-size:11px;color:#3fb950;margin-top:4px}
nav{position:sticky;top:0;background:#0d1117;padding:10px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #30363d;z-index:9}
nav a{color:#58a6ff;margin-right:12px;text-decoration:none;font-size:13px}
.stat{display:inline-block;background:#161b22;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 18px;margin:4px;text-align:center}
.stat b{font-size:22px;color:#3fb950;display:block}
.toc{background:#161b22;border:1px solid #30363d;border-radius:8px;padding:16px;margin:16px 0}
.toc a{color:#79c0ff;text-decoration:none;display:block;padding:3px 0}
</style></head><body>
<h1>🛡️ CYBERSECURITY MASTER KNOWLEDGE BASE</h1>
<div class="stat"><b>142</b>Topics</div>
<div class="stat"><b>8</b>Sections</div>
<div class="stat"><b>64</b>Levels</div>
<nav><div class="toc"><a href="#s1">1-Hacker Classifications (8)</a><a href="#s2">2-Disciplines (28)</a><a href="#s3">3-Attack Vectors (23)</a><a href="#s4">4-Languages (12)</a><a href="#s5">5-Operating Systems (17)</a><a href="#s6">6-Tools (23)</a><a href="#s7">7-Networking (19)</a><a href="#s8">8-Advanced (12)</a></div></nav><h2 id="s1">1-Hacker Classifications <span style="color:#8b949e;font-size:14px">(8)</span></h2><div class="grid"><div class="card">
<div class="nm">White Hat<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Ethical</span></div>
<div class="mt">Authorized security testing, bug bounty, pentesting</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> scope, authorization, disclosure</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> rules of engagement, signed contracts</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Black Hat<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Criminal</span></div>
<div class="mt">Unauthorized intrusion, malware, theft</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> exploit kits, C2, persistence</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> EDR, MFA, patching, least privilege</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Grey Hat<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Mixed</span></div>
<div class="mt">Finds vulns then discloses for reward/fame</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> vulnerability disclosure, extortion</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> bug bounty programs, safe harbor</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Red Hat<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Vigilante</span></div>
<div class="mt">Attacks black hats, hack-back operations</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> hack-back, doxxing, vigilante justice</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> legal risk — hack-back is illegal in most jurisdictions</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Blue Hat<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Microsoft term</span></div>
<div class="mt">Security consultants testing Windows pre-release</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> MSRC, trusted testing</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> vendor trust programs</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Green Hat<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Novice</span></div>
<div class="mt">Beginner learning security, script kiddies evolving</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> CTFs, labs, training</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> legal labs only, certifications</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Purple Team<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Collaborative</span></div>
<div class="mt">Red team + blue team working together</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> attack simulation + detection engineering</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> purple teaming exercises</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Yellow Hat<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Informal</span></div>
<div class="mt">Ethical hackers in Chinese/Russian communities</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> mutually inconsistent usage</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> not standardized — verify context</div></div></div><h2 id="s2">2-Disciplines <span style="color:#8b949e;font-size:14px">(28)</span></h2><div class="grid"><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Ethical Hacking<span class="lv" style="background:#58a6ff">Foundation</span></div>
<div class="mt">Authorized vulnerability discovery and exploitation</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> scope, ROE, reporting</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> authorization, methodology (PTES/OSSTMM)</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Penetration Testing<span class="lv" style="background:#f85149">Offensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Simulated attacks to find weaknesses</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> recon, exploitation, post-ex, reporting</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> rules of engagement, client authorization</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Network Security<span class="lv" style="background:#3fb950">Defensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Protecting network infrastructure</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> firewalls, IDS/IPS, segmentation</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> defense in depth, monitoring</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Web App Security<span class="lv" style="background:#f85149">Offensive+Defensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Securing web applications</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> OWASP Top 10, input validation</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> WAF, secure coding, testing</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">API Security<span class="lv" style="background:#d29922">Specialized</span></div>
<div class="mt">Securing API endpoints</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> authN/Z, rate limiting, input validation</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> OAuth2, JWT, API gateways</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Cloud Security<span class="lv" style="background:#d29922">Specialized</span></div>
<div class="mt">AWS/Azure/GCP security</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> IAM, shared responsibility, misconfig</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> CSPM, least privilege, encryption</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Mobile Security<span class="lv" style="background:#d29922">Specialized</span></div>
<div class="mt">iOS/Android app security</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> reverse engineering, runtime analysis</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> code obfuscation, cert pinning, MDM</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">OS Security<span class="lv" style="background:#58a6ff">Foundation</span></div>
<div class="mt">Kernel, permissions, process isolation</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> DAC/MAC, sandboxing, SELinux</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> hardening, patching, least privilege</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Database Security<span class="lv" style="background:#d29922">Specialized</span></div>
<div class="mt">Protecting data stores</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> encryption at rest, access control, injection</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> parameterized queries, auditing</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Hardware Security<span class="lv" style="background:#bc8cff">Advanced</span></div>
<div class="mt">Physical/firmware security</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> TPM, secure boot, side channels</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> hardware roots of trust</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Wireless Security<span class="lv" style="background:#d29922">Specialized</span></div>
<div class="mt">WiFi/BT/Zigbee security</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> WPA2/3, deauth, evil twin</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> strong passwords, 802.1X, monitoring</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Cryptography<span class="lv" style="background:#58a6ff">Foundation</span></div>
<div class="mt">Encryption, hashing, signatures</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> symmetric/asymmetric, PKI, protocols</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> algorithm agility, key management</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Malware Analysis<span class="lv" style="background:#3fb950">Defensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Understanding malicious software</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> static/dynamic analysis, sandboxing</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> AV, EDR, threat intel</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Reverse Engineering<span class="lv" style="background:#bc8cff">Advanced</span></div>
<div class="mt">Decompiling binaries, understanding software</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> disassembly, decompilation, debugging</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> legal frameworks, clean rooms</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Exploit Development<span class="lv" style="background:#bc8cff">Advanced</span></div>
<div class="mt">Writing exploits for vulnerabilities</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> memory corruption, ROP, shellcode</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> patching, ASLR, DEP, CET</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Vulnerability Research<span class="lv" style="background:#bc8cff">Advanced</span></div>
<div class="mt">Finding 0-days in software</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> fuzzing, code audit, variant analysis</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> responsible disclosure, bug bounty</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Digital Forensics<span class="lv" style="background:#3fb950">Defensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Investigating incidents post-breach</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> memory/disk analysis, timeline</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> chain of custody, tools (Volatility, Autopsy)</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Incident Response<span class="lv" style="background:#3fb950">Defensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Containing and recovering from breaches</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> detection, containment, eradication</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> IR plans, playbooks, forensics</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Threat Intelligence<span class="lv" style="background:#3fb950">Defensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Collecting/analyzing threat data</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> IOCs, TTPs, attribution</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> threat feeds, ISACs</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Social Engineering<span class="lv" style="background:#f85149">Offensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Manipulating humans</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> phishing, pretexting, vishing</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> security awareness, verification</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">IAM<span class="lv" style="background:#3fb950">Defensive</span></div>
<div class="mt">Identity and access management</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> SSO, MFA, RBAC, PAM</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> zero trust, least privilege</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Zero Trust<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Architecture</span></div>
<div class="mt">Never trust, always verify</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> microsegmentation, continuous auth</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> ZTNA, identity-centric</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">AppSec<span class="lv" style="background:#79c0ff">Engineering</span></div>
<div class="mt">Secure software development</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> SDLC, threat modeling, SAST/DAST</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> shift-left security, DevSecOps</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Supply Chain Security<span class="lv" style="background:#39c5cf">Emerging</span></div>
<div class="mt">Dependencies, build systems, vendors</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> SBOM, SLSA, dependency confusion</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> provenance, signing, vetting</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">AI Security<span class="lv" style="background:#39c5cf">Emerging</span></div>
<div class="mt">Attacks on/with AI systems</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> prompt injection, model theft, adversarial</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> guardrails, red teaming, monitoring</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">IoT Security<span class="lv" style="background:#d29922">Specialized</span></div>
<div class="mt">Embedded/connected device security</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> firmware analysis, default creds</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> network segmentation, updates</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Critical Infrastructure<span class="lv" style="background:#f0883e">National</span></div>
<div class="mt">Power grid, water, transport</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> ICS/SCADA, safety systems</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> air gaps, safety instrumented systems</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Blockchain Security<span class="lv" style="background:#39c5cf">Emerging</span></div>
<div class="mt">Smart contracts, wallets, DeFi</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> smart contract bugs, key management</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> audits, formal verification, multisig</div></div></div><h2 id="s3">3-Attack Vectors <span style="color:#8b949e;font-size:14px">(23)</span></h2><div class="grid"><div class="card">
<div class="nm">SQL Injection<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Web</span></div>
<div class="mt">Malicious SQL in input fields</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> UNION, blind, time-based, error-based</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> parameterized queries, input validation, WAF</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">XSS<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Web</span></div>
<div class="mt">JavaScript injection into pages</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> reflected, stored, DOM-based</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> output encoding, CSP, sanitization</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">CSRF<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Web</span></div>
<div class="mt">Forged requests using victim&#x27;s session</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> state-changing actions</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> CSRF tokens, SameSite cookies</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">RCE<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">General</span></div>
<div class="mt">Remote code execution</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> command injection, deserialization</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> input validation, sandboxing</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Buffer Overflow<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Memory</span></div>
<div class="mt">Overwriting memory bounds</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> stack/heap overflow, format strings</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> bounds checking, ASLR, DEP, canaries</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Privilege Escalation<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">System</span></div>
<div class="mt">Gaining higher access</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> kernel exploits, misconfig, sudo abuse</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> least privilege, patching, monitoring</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Auth Bypass<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">General</span></div>
<div class="mt">Skipping authentication</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> logic flaws, JWT attacks, default creds</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> MFA, secure session mgmt, rate limiting</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Session Hijacking<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Web</span></div>
<div class="mt">Stealing session tokens</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> XSS, sniffing, fixation</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> secure cookies, HTTPS, token rotation</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">DNS Spoofing<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Network</span></div>
<div class="mt">Fake DNS responses</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> cache poisoning, pharming</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> DNSSEC, DoH, monitoring</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">IP Spoofing<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Network</span></div>
<div class="mt">Faking source IP</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> UDP-based attacks, SYN floods</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> ingress filtering, TCP</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">MITM<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Network</span></div>
<div class="mt">Intercepting communication</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> ARP spoofing, rogue AP, SSL stripping</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> TLS, cert pinning, VPN</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Phishing<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Social</span></div>
<div class="mt">Deceptive messages for credentials</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> spear phishing, whaling, clone sites</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> training, email filtering, MFA</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Credential Stuffing<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Auth</span></div>
<div class="mt">Using leaked creds on other sites</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> breach databases, automation</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> MFA, rate limiting, breach monitoring</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Brute Force<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Auth</span></div>
<div class="mt">Trying all combinations</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> password guessing, PIN cracking</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> rate limiting, lockouts, MFA</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">DoS<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Network</span></div>
<div class="mt">Overwhelming service</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> SYN flood, application-layer</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> rate limiting, CDN, anycast</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">DDoS<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Network</span></div>
<div class="mt">Distributed DoS</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> botnets, amplification</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> DDoS protection, scrubbing, upstream filtering</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Malware/Ransomware<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Endpoint</span></div>
<div class="mt">Malicious software</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> trojans, ransomware, wipers</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> AV, EDR, backups, patching</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Rootkits<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Endpoint</span></div>
<div class="mt">Deep system compromise</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> kernel-level hiding</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> secure boot, integrity checks, EDR</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Keyloggers<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Endpoint</span></div>
<div class="mt">Recording keystrokes</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> hardware/software</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> EDR, input encryption, awareness</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Supply Chain<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Software</span></div>
<div class="mt">Compromising dependencies</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> typosquatting, dependency confusion</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> SBOM, pinning, vetting</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Zero-Day<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Research</span></div>
<div class="mt">Unknown unpatched vuln</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> n-day research, 1-day exploits</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> patching, WAF, defense in depth</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Misconfiguration<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Cloud/Server</span></div>
<div class="mt">Insecure defaults</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> open buckets, default passwords</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> CSPM, hardening baselines</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Insecure API<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Web</span></div>
<div class="mt">API vulnerabilities</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> missing auth, excessive data</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> API gateways, rate limits, testing</div></div></div><h2 id="s4">4-Languages <span style="color:#8b949e;font-size:14px">(12)</span></h2><div class="grid"><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Python<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Most versatile</span></div>
<div class="mt">Automation, scripting, security tools, ML</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> pwntools, scapy, requests</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> all disciplines</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">C<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Systems/memory</span></div>
<div class="mt">Kernel, drivers, exploit dev</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> pointers, memory control</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> exploit dev, RE, OS</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">C++<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Systems</span></div>
<div class="mt">Complex software, malware</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> templates, performance</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> malware analysis, tools</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Rust<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Modern systems</span></div>
<div class="mt">Safe systems programming</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> memory safety, performance</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> security tools, kernel</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Assembly<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Lowest level</span></div>
<div class="mt">Shellcode, reversing</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> direct hardware control</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> exploit dev, RE</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Java<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Enterprise</span></div>
<div class="mt">Enterprise apps, Android</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> JVM, bytecode</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> web security, mobile</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">JavaScript<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Web</span></div>
<div class="mt">Frontend, Node.js backend</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> XSS, DOM manipulation</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> web security</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">PHP<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Web legacy</span></div>
<div class="mt">Web applications</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> server-side scripting</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> web security</div></div><div class="card">
<div class="nm">Go<span class="lv" style="background:#8b949e">Modern systems</span></div>
<div class="mt">Network tools, cloud-native</div>
<div class="kc"><b>Key:</b> concurrency, performance</div>
<div class="df"><b>Defense:</b> network security, cloud</div></div><div class="card">
